COMPLIANCE:
Scene ID: SC_002_006
Allowed events: Artie realizes his exploit, Fizz comments on the system error, Artie farms skeletons with pebbles, Artie levels up, the room fills with loot.
Forbidden milestones: None explicitly forbidden, but must not advance beyond clearing the antechamber.

Current arm-side / inventory facts: Cloak of the Cowardly Lion (equipped, shoulders), Rusty Iron Dagger (stowed, belt), Employee ID Badge (equipped, neck_lanyard), Participation Trophy (equipped, lapel), Leather Wallet (stowed, pocket_right).

Durable changes committed: Artie's XP increased to 905, Level 3 achieved, Stamina increased to 12, Stat Points increased to 10. Aggro status removed.

APPEARANCE_CHECK:
- CHAR_ARTIE: messy brown hair, pale skin, skinny fat build
- CHAR_FIZZ: neon pink glowing hair, translucent ethereal build

PROSE:
Artie stared at the massive loot pile burying the shattered remains of the first skeleton, a slow, greedy realization dawning on him. If a single pebble could do that, he had just stumbled onto a highly repeatable exploit. He scooped up a handful of gravel, eyeing the other shambling skeletons in the antechamber.

"Did you catch the math on that?" Artie muttered, still half-expecting the system to ban him. "The rock triggered a 99,999 damage critical hit, instantly shattering the skeleton."

Fizz zipped over the mountain of gold coins and glowing bone fragments, her digital eyes wide. "It's a cascading math failure," she said, her voice dropping to a conspiratorial whisper. "The massive overkill damage caused a system error, forcing the skeleton to drop its entire loot table at once. The engine literally panicked and dumped everything."

Artie grinned. His 1/1 HP was a terrifying liability, but right now? It was the key to the kingdom. He adjusted the oversized Cloak of the Cowardly Lion on his shoulders, making sure it didn't snag on his arm, and checked that his Rusty Iron Dagger was securely stowed at his belt. He wouldn't need the blade. He had rocks.

He wound up and lobbed a jagged piece of crypt masonry at a skeleton limping toward him from the shadows. The rock pinged off the monster's skull with a pathetic *clack*.

`[Critical Hit! -99,999 HP]`
`[Target Defeated.]`

The skeleton exploded into a shower of white light. A second later, the air filled with the heavy clinking of currency and the clatter of useless low-level gear.

`[Experience Gained: 150 XP]`
`[Loot Drop: 42 Gold Coins, 14 Bone Fragments, 1 Rusty Iron Helm, 2 Minor Stamina Potions, 1 Skeletal Femur, 1 Tattered Tunic...]`

"Oh, this is beautiful," Artie laughed, side-stepping a rolling skull. He threw another rock. Then another.

`[Critical Hit! -99,999 HP]`
`[Target Defeated.]`
`[Experience Gained: 150 XP]`

He developed a rhythm. Chuck a pebble, watch the skeleton vaporize, dodge the incoming avalanche of loot. The antechamber quickly transformed from a gloomy, damp crypt into a glittering hazard zone. He had to be careful not to trip over the knee-deep piles of copper and silver, or the sheer volume of rusty iron swords threatening to impale him. With his 1 HP, stubbing his toe on a discarded breastplate could be lethal.

`[Experience Gained: 150 XP]`
`[Experience Gained: 150 XP]`
`[Level Up! You are now Level 2.]`
`[Level Up! You are now Level 3.]`

Artie paused, panting slightly as the golden glow of leveling washed over him. He opened his stat sheet.

`[HP: 1/1 (Locked)]`
`[Stamina: 12/12]`
`[Stat Points Available: 10]`

"Still locked at one HP," Artie sighed, dismissing the window. "But the stamina bump is nice."

"You're destabilizing the local instance," Fizz warned, hovering above a particularly tall stack of iron shields. "The physics engine is struggling to render all these individual coins. If you keep this up, the lag might kill you before a monster does."

"Just one more," Artie said, spotting a final Skeletal Guard cowering in the corner. It actually looked like it was trying to merge with the stone wall to avoid him. Artie flicked a tiny chip of gravel.

`[Critical Hit! -99,999 HP]`
`[Target Defeated.]`
`[Experience Gained: 150 XP]`

A fresh geyser of loot erupted, cascading across the floor and burying the last patch of visible cobblestone. Artie stood amidst a ridiculous mountain of loot, having cleared the room of every last threat in the antechamber.

